# Shell layout (frozen)

Canonical spec: **`docs/LAYOUT.md`** (status: 已冻结).

## Six layers (order fixed)

`Header` → `Title` (1 row) → `Catalog` (1 row) → `Body` → `Message` (1 row) → `Footer`

- Do **not** add/remove/reorder layers, merge Title+Catalog, or drop Message without **explicit user confirmation**.
- Do **not** change `Get-ShellLayoutConstants` / row math in `Layout.ps1` without confirmation.
- Use only standard layer names: **Header / Title / Catalog / Body / Message / Footer** and matching symbols (`CatalogRow`, `BodyCatalogLine`, `LayoutLineMetrics`, …).

## Allowed without layout approval

- Fill Catalog/Message text; Body list/content; i18n; bug fixes that preserve row budget.
- `ListLayout.ps1` column widths (Body internals).

## Required before layout changes

1. Cite which layer(s) and constants would change.
2. Ask user to confirm modifying `docs/LAYOUT.md` and/or layout implementation.
3. If user did not explicitly request a layout change, keep existing six-layer structure.

Footer Esc/exit rules remain in `shell-toolbar.mdc`.
